# /../helpers.ts
Place methods that are used more than once from a container/component here
Some examples include 
Getting Progress colours
```ts
export const getProgressColor = (progress: number) => {
  if (progress < 60) {
    return '#808080';
  }
  if (progress >= 60 && progress < 80) {
    return '#f6be16';
  }
  if (progress >= 80) {
    return '#e7103b';
  }
};
```

Refer to the shared folder for some global shared helpers [helpers](../../src/_shared/utils/helpers.tsx) instead of writing new ones with the same functionality
Commonly used ones include 

isValidNumber - uses lodash to check if arg is a number, is not NaN, and is finite (will allow 0 through)
convertUnit - convertor for B to PB, backwards compatible as well (PB to B)
toSafeNumber - leverages isValidNumber to render 0 for invalid numbers
numberToDisplayString - leverages isValidNumber to render '-' for invalid numbers, importantly also renders without trailing 0s for decimal values

# /../s.module.less
**USE** .less instead of .scss going forward, but feel free to reference css stylings from .scss files
The change is due to pure .less changes updating the page without refreshes, unlike .scss